OBSERVATIONS (backlog, not FAILs):
 O1. A consequence of the manifests/ extension: when manifests/ cannot be listed or is not a directory (a regular file or a dangling link at that path), escalate-scan flags EVERY ledger row, including a pending row with no manifests ("flag: u -> tier 3 (critical-glob-unreadable)"). For the regular-file and dangling-link cases this departs from the literal parenthetical in pinned 1 ("a row that has not started is never flagged"). There is also a mode-100 (x-only) manifests/ where base could still accept a tier-1/2 row and the new gate refuses it. All of these are corrupt .swarm layouts. The lead should decide whether to pin it.
 O2. A python3 replacement that exits 12 with no stdout produces "gate: critical-glob evaluation unreadable: " with an empty detail. Only a shim can do this; the real evaluator always prints a path or "evaluator failed".
 O3. At tier 3 the diagnostic line is still printed on stderr at check and escalate-scan, although nothing is blocked. This is consistent with "one line per unreadable evaluation".
 O4. Pre-existing and fixed here: base parse() blocks forever on a FIFO at the CURRENT manifest (readFileSync). Pre-existing and unchanged: invalid UTF-8 in the CURRENT manifest at tier 3 gives the gate FAIL "manifest path '\xff' has no fingerprint line"; parse agrees.
